{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I checked your account from our end. Your account is active, VPN access is on, and your Duo sign-in is set up. Your VPN connected from Lisbon successfully on each of the last three days, so the problem is most likely with the hotel Wi-Fi or the laptop's VPN app today. Please try these steps: 1) Open a web browser and go to any public website. If the hotel's sign-in page appears, complete it, then try again. 2) Fully quit the VPN app, restart your laptop, and open the VPN app again. 3) Connect and approve the Duo push on your phone. If you still can't connect, please reply with the exact error message the VPN shows, whether the Duo notification arrives, and the time you tried. We'll pick it up from there. Since you need the shared drive for your presentation, you can also try connecting from the hotel's mobile hotspot on your phone if the Wi-Fi keeps blocking the VPN.",
  "internal_note": "Checked EVAL-net-01 (Leo Martins, user_id 6, BL-LT-0106). Account active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0. Duo enrolled (duo_push on phone). Sign-in logs: VPN sign-ins from Lisbon on Oct 8, 9, and 10 all succeeded with Duo push from residential IP 198.51.100.66. No failed_password or mfa_denied entries in the 14-day window, so the failing attempt today either never reached the server or is not logged. Likely client-side or hotel Wi-Fi captive portal, per KB-013 fix 3 and 4. Not escalating yet because the account and Duo are healthy and no attempts show server-side failures. Asked user for the exact error and whether the Duo push arrives. If the user returns with failures that reach the server, or with a Duo push that never arrives after refresh, re-check logs and consider Tier 2. No actions queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-016"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
